  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sahara Expo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sahara Expo, the International Agricultural Exhibition for Africa and the Middle East, is the main platform for agriculture, animal production, and aquaculture in the Middle East and Northern Africa (MENA) region. In the combi-track, a Dutch pavilion and trade mission on climate and water smart agriculture to the Sahara Expo, was included in the activities.The combi-track &quot;Climate and Water Smart Agriculture (CaWSA)&quot; focuses on linking Egyptian, Dutch, and international companies, entrepreneurs and institutes, fostering trade, innovation, and entrepreneurship in the area of climate and water smart agriculture. This combi-track works towards a resilient, future-proof farming system in Egypt, in which farmers, youth and women in particular, thrive.The goal of this project is to participate with a Dutch pavilion at the Sahara Expo with Dutch horticulture and agro-food companies, as well as governmental and knowledge institutes. This will create the following opportunities:&#x2022;	Business opportunities between Dutch companies and Egyptian or MENA companies;&#x2022;	Knowledge exchange between Egyptian and Dutch companies and knowledge institutions on climate and water smart agriculture via a 3-day seminar programme;&#x2022;	Enhanced possibilities for further cooperation;&#x2022;	Promotion of selected Dutch funded programs and activities in the agriculture sector in Egypt and identifications of new partnerships and activities between the Netherlands and Egypt, and the MENA region by extension, in the field of agriculture and horticulture under the Dutch combi-track approach;&#x2022;	Positioning of the Netherlands, and its companies, as the partner in sustainable, innovative, climate smart and circular agriculture and horticulture.</narrative>
  </description>
